Final presentation Part B ( instruction )



INSTRUCTIONS
Students will work in groups in order to develop a data science project that leverages AWS Cloud Services.

The grade of final project will be based on the following items:

-Presentation
-Demo
-Project architecture
-The final project will have the following components:

Project Definition where the students will define in detail:
-Scope of the project
-Features that will be implemented
-Data sources (from where you will get the data)
-Expected outcomes


Project Architecture where the students will define:
-Logical architecture of the project indicating AWS cloud services that will be used and their roles in the architecture
-Data flow indicating how data will be ingested, clean up, processed, and released
-Project Implementation where students will demonstrate their solution by showing:
-Cloud services in action
-Inputs and outputs consumed and produced, respectively
-Project presentation where students will present their projects

All the project artifacts, including presentations, must be uploaded into a GitHub account.
Students must submit a video doing the presentation. Both video and ppt (presentation) must be submitted via blackboard and must also be available in the GitHub.

AT LEAST ONE GROUP member must present the project during the class.
The presentations including the video with the demo cannot be longer than 15 min so all groups would have a chance to present.
